The Phoenicians inhabited the coastal plain which is 
today Lebanon, with their two major port cities of 
Sidon and Tyre. They were the most enterprising traders 
and seafarers in the Mediterranean, with a relatively 
high level of affluence and skills. Hiram, king of Tyre, 
had been the friend and business partner of David and 
Solomon, and Omni had renewed these ties with the 
contemporary Phoenician ruler Ethbaal. The alliance 
was cemented by Ahab’s marriage to Ethbaal’s 
daughter Jezebel. 

