among his followers they broke off the engagement and 
retreated back across the river and up to Samaria. Here 
Ahab was buried, ‘And they washed the chariot by the 
pool of Samaria, and the dogs licked up his blood.’ 
(1 Kgs. 22:38) He was succeeded by his son Ahaziah. 
