The old man was deceived and bestowed the blessing on 
Jacob, declaring that he would be the head of the family 
after Isaac’s death and his brethren would serve him. 

When Esau returned and learnt what had happened, 
he wept bitterly, and begged his father to bless him as 
well. Isaac replied that Esau would have to serve his 
brother Jacob, but promised that Esau too would pros- 
per and in due course become independent. Esau, his 
father added, would live by the sword. 


