with the Feast of Purim: ‘Therefore the Jews of the 
villages, who live in the open towns, hold the fourteenth 
day of the month of Adar as a day for gladness and 
feasting and holiday-making, and a day on which they 
send choice portions to one another.’ (Esther 9:19) (In 
walled cities the feast was held a day later because in 
Susa the fighting had lasted two days.) [Book of Esther] 
