to Isaac with Jacob pretending to be Esau. To make 
the deception more effective, she covered Jacob’s 
smooth hands and neck with bits of the fleece of the 
slain kids (for Esau was a hairy man) and she put 
Esau’s garment on Jacob. Isaac was suspicious at first, 
saying, ‘The voice is Jacob’s voice, but the hands are 
