Esau came in with the venison he had prepared for 
his father, and Isaac realized he had been deceived. 
But he could not now take back the blessing bestowed 
on Jacob. Esau, wailing with anger and grief, pressed 
Isaac to bless him as well. The old man replied that 
Esau would have to serve Jacob, but he too would 
prosper and become independent. 

Fearing that Esau would kill Jacob in revenge, 
Rebekah persuaded Isaac to send Jacob to her brother 
Laban in Haran so that he too should marry someone 
of his own kin. 

