Jerusalem from the Babylonian troops. They were a 
fundamentalist sect of desert nomads, living by the 
injunctions of an ancestor Jonadab, the son of Rehab, 
that they should not live in houses, till the soil or touch 
wine. Jeremiah tested them by bringing them into a 
chamber of the Temple and offering them glasses of 
wine which were rejected. He then held them up as an 


