asylum by the Pharaoh Shishak. 

On Solomon’s death his son Rehoboam succeeded 
to the throne. The northern tribes seceded, setting up 
a separate kingdom of Israel. Jeroboam returned from 
Egypt and was elected its first ruler. The great Hebrew 
realm of David and Solomon had broken up into two 
small and quarrelling successor states. 

Jeroboam at first resided in Shechem. After a period 
at Penuel across the Jordan river, he set up his perman- 





