condemned the king beside the altar at Bethel, on which 
burnt-offerings had just been made. Jeroboam pointed 
at the man and ordered him to be arrested, but the 
king’s outstretched arm became paralysed and he could 
not move it. At the same moment the altar flew apart 
and the ashes on it were scattered to the winds. The 
