palace guard, sought him out there and killed him, 
‘and he was buried in his own house in the wilderness’ 
(1 Kgs. 2:34). Thus Joab paid with his blood for his 
deeds of violence, and for wavering at the end in his 
lifelong devotion to David. [1 Sam. 26:6; 2 Sam. 2:13- 
