It is a moot point how much of the land of Canaan 
was actually conquered and occupied by the Israelites 
in Joshua’s time. In one passage it is claimed that 
‘Joshua took the whole land, according to all that the 
Lord had spoken to Moses; and Joshua gave it for an 
inheritance to Israel according to their tribal allotments. 
And the land had rest from war.’ (Josh. 11:23) But this 
statement was more rhetorical than factual. That the 
conquest was neither rapid nor complete is clear from 


