third day they gathered before the mountain that was 
covered with a thick cloud. Out of it came thunder, 
lightning and the loud blasts of a trumpet. ‘And Mount 
Sinai was wrapped in smoke, because the Lord descend- 
ed upon it in fire; and the smoke of it went up like the 
smoke of a kiln, and the whole mountain quaked 
greatly.” (Exod. 19:18) Then the voice of God rolled 
forth, solemnly pronouncing the Ten Commandments: 

