At their next camping place Aaron and Miriam 
started speaking against Moses, of whom they had 
become jealous. The Lord was angry at this attack, and 
Miriam was stricken with leprosy. Moses prayed that 
she be forgiven, and she recovered after seven days of 
isolation in the desert outside the camp. Oddly enough 
Aaron was not punished — perhaps because of his 
priestly role. 

