Assyrian provinces, with governors stationed at 
Megiddo {for the Galilee), Dor (for the coast), and 
Gilead, east of the Jordan river. Many of the inhabitants 
of these territories were taken away to Assyria as 
captives. All that was left intact of Israel was the capital 


