Samson’s birth, like that of a number of Bible heroes, 
had a miraculous aspect. His father Manoah lived in the 
village of Zorah, situated in the undulating foothill 
region of the Shephelah. It overlooked the valley of 
Sorek (through which the railway line now climbs up 
to Jerusalem). 

His mother was a pious woman who had been child- 
less for many years. One day an angel appeared before 
her and told her she would conceive a son. He warned 
her not to drink wine or eat unclean food during her 
pregnancy. The child would be dedicated to God’s 
Service, and forbidden to cut his hair or touch strong 
drink. The prophecy was added that when he grew up, 
he would ‘begin to deliver Israel from the hand of the 
Philistines’ (Judg. 13:5). 

