From now on David was a fugitive from the king. 
He found refuge in the mountain caves of Adullam, 
south-west of Jerusalem, and became the leader of a 
band of about four hundred outcasts. When Saul 
heard that David had slipped out of his hands, he 
railed bitterly at his attendants and accused everyone 
of disloyalty, including Jonathan. Hearing the priests 
of the Shrine of Nob had helped David, he had them 
