The ‘Lachish Letters’ 

The remarkable ‘Lachish Letters’ relating to the Baby- 
lonian invasion of Judah at the beginning of the 6th 
century BC, were discovered at the archaeological exca- 
vations of the fortified Judean city of Lachish (Tel ed- 
Duweir) carried out between 1932 and 1938. Eighteen 
ostraca — inscribed potsherds — were found among the 
burnt debris in a guard-room of a bastion in the outer 
city wall. Three more were found elsewhere on the site. 





