‘and learn that this city 1s a rebellious city, hurtful to 
kings and provinces...’ (Ezra 4:15). The palace accepted 
this plea, and orders were given that the work was to be 
suspended. 

Eighteen years later, after King Darius 1 had mounted 
the Persian throne, Zerubbabel and Jeshua called the 
