Among the Apocrypha are two short works con- 
taining additional legends about the prophet Daniel — 
the story of Susanna; and Bel and the Dragon. They 
were originally written in Hebrew or Aramaic in the 
second century Bc. These two works were included in 
the Septuagint (Greek Bible) and later in the Vulgate 
(Catholic Bible), where they were added to the Book 
of Daniel as Chapters 13 and 14. 

