The work known as the Wisdom of Jesus the son of 
Sirach (or Joshua Ben Sira in the Hebrew form) was 
originally written in Hebrew in Palestine, early in the 
2nd century BC. From the 3rd century AD the book 
also became known in the Christian church as ‘Eccle- 
siasticus’, a Latin word that simply means ‘church 
