name of the king ordering provincial governors to give 
the Jews arms for self-defence. 

In a final passage, Mordecai recalls his dream, and 
praises the Lord for safeguarding the Jews. 

The object of these additions was clearly to inject a 
religious note lacking in the canonical story of Esther. 
see also MORDECAI (O.T. section) [Ad. Est. 11:2-12; 12; 
