severe famine, which actually occurred in the reign of 
the Emperor Claudius. In fact there were acute short- 
ages of food in different parts of the Roman Empire over 
the period of years 41—54. Josephus, the Jewish historian, 
relates that there was a famine in Jerusalem during the 
procuratorship of Tiberias Alexander and that the 
poor were relieved by the generosity of Queen Helena of 
Adiabene between the years 46 and 48. 


