In consequence, they instigated the crowd to accuse 
him of blasphemy against Moses and God, for the Jew 
the ultimate wickedness. The mob dragged Stephen off 
to the Council and accused him of speaking both against 
the Temple, as the official centre of worship, and against 
the Law. Members of the synagogue of the Alexandrians 
