One of the proconsul’s household was a Jewish magician 
called Elymas Bar-Jesus, who tried to prevent the preach- 
ing of the Christian gospel to his master. Paul very 
quickly and mercilessly exposed him, and the proconsul 
accepted Paul’s teaching about Jesus. 

Crossing over to the mainland of Pisidia, on the south 
coast of Asia Minor, they landed at Attalia and set off 
inland, climbing the western spurs of the rugged Taurus 
range, infested with robbers and other hazards. A few 
miles inland, John Mark (see MARK) left them and re- 
turned to Jerusalem. The rest arrived at Antioch, the 
capital of Pisidia — not of Syria —a hundred miles north 
