(John 11 :49-53) 

No doubt the outcome of their consultations was a 
very clever and crafty solution, possibly the product of 
the fertile cunning of Caiaphas himself. This was to 
hand Jesus over to the Roman authorities: in any case 
they could not execute him. They could, however, label 
him guilty of treason and a danger to the imperial 


