Among the Roman symbols, two have particular 
significance for the Christian. The first is the regimental 
crest of the Tenth Legion, two eagles back to back and 
beak to beak. The second is the Roman army’s equiva- 
lent of the Victoria Cross: it was awarded to a soldier 
who saved the life of an officer in battle. It is a victor’s 
