in Athens, and brought him to speak publicly on the 
Aeropagus, during his Second Journey in the years 50-2. 

The Epicureans followed the teachings of a Greek 
thinker called Epicurus, 342-270 Bc, who claimed that 
reality lay in the world of nature rather than in the 


