stretch for miles across the country; their bridges and 
their roads survive as memorials of the past. 

We know of at least one visit of Jesus to the territory 
of the Ten Towns, on which occasion he cured the man 
whose name was Legion, gave speech to the deaf mute, 
and fed the five thousand. [Rom. 1:14, 16; 10:12; Gal. 
2:3: 3:28; Colf3a4: John 12:20; Acts 14:1; 17:4, 12; 
