in the year 53. In about the year 60, Paul appeared 
before Agrippa at the request of Festus, the Roman 
procurator, who wished to draw up the charges against 
Paul before sending him to Rome. 

Luke’s account in Acts gives some indication of the 
respect in which Agrippa was held by both Romans and 
Jews. Festus lays Paul’s case before Agrippa with much 


