to place the responsibility for the death of Jesus on the 
shoulders of Pilate, claiming that he himself is a loyal 
supporter of the Roman administration. He wants to 
make the case of Jesus seem to be similar to that of any 
other self-appointed leader of an uprising against 
authority. In the Gospel of Luke the crowd, incited by 
the chief priests, demands the release of Barabbas, ‘a 
