Only the author of the Gospel of Luke relates the story 
of the ascension of Jesus Christ into heaven from the 
Mount of Olives. In the Gospel he writes, ‘Then he led 
them out as far as Bethany, and lifting up his hand he 
blessed them. While he blessed them, he parted from 
them.’ In the Acts of the Apostles there is more des- 
cription, ‘And when he had said this, as they were 
looking on, he was lifted up, and a cloud took him from 
their sight ... they were gazing up into heaven as he 
went. ... Then they returned to Jerusalem from the 
