scholar Jerome, have suggested that the normal Greek 
words used for ‘brothers’ and ‘sisters’ could be intended 
to include ‘cousins’. It must be admitted that oriental 
customs can be quoted to support this. However, we 
may see a purpose in the selection of the words used. 

Mark, no doubt followed by Matthew and Luke, 
describes Jesus teaching at Capernaum and, hearing 
that his mother and brothers have arrived and are 
asking for him, he replied, ‘“‘Who are my mother and 
my brothers?’ Looking around on those who sat about 
him, he said, ‘“‘Here are my mother and my brothers! 
