trying to force Jesus’s hand to declare his Messiahship, 
for nationalistic motives, or was simply jealous, as a 
shrewd southerner, of his rustic Galilean rivals, such as 
Peter and John, we may never Know. We may be sure, 
however, that Judas was no puppet predestined to play 
a necessary part in the betrayal of Jesus. Judas was 
essentially a free agent, acting from his own motives at 
any given moment. 

