Pharisees to say whether it was lawful to do good on 
such a day. He allowed his disciples to pluck and rub 
ears of corn, thus technically reaping and threshing on 
the Sabbath day (Mark 2:23-6). He justified his actions 
by declaring, ‘The sabbath was made for man, not 
