yet another function of the Pavement, whose water 
runnels still lead down into the cavernous vaults below, 
where cistern-tops yet bear the marks of lock and 
chain, and whose counter-weights and pulleys are still 
to be seen. 

On to this Pavement prisoner and escort proceeded, 
while the crowd, for fear of defilement before Passover, 
crammed by the thousand into the great double gate- 
