and asks for help and good wishes. First, however, he 
has to take the money contributed by the Christians in 
Greece to Jerusalem. It was appropriate, Paul said, that 
the Greeks — spiritual debtors to the Jewish-Christians — 
should contribute to their material needs. As soon as he 





