SIMEON (Heb., Gk. ‘hearing’) 1. Simeon, the priest 
The first-born son of every Jewish family had to be 
presented within the Temple at Jerusalem forty days 
after birth. In earlier, pagan times, the first son had 
often been sacrificed to the tribal god, as the first- 
fruit of the family. Now the Hebrew Law had adapted 
this primitive custom by demanding the offering of 


