tion. Matthew and Luke describe him as of Cyrene, 
part of Libya in North Africa. Mark records that he 
was the father of Alexander and Rufus, rather as though 
these two sons had become Christians and were known 
to his readers, perhaps in Rome. Luke and Mark both 
say that Simon of Cyrene had ‘come in from the coun- 


