SPIRIT OF GOD The Holy Spirit is the life and 
activity of God at work in the world of nature and also 
in and through people. The Hebrew word for ‘spirit’ is 
the same as that for ‘breath’ or ‘wind’, and can even 
imply ‘life’, just as the English word ‘spirit’ forms the 
root of others, such as ‘inspire’, ‘expire’, and ‘respira- 
tion’, meaning ‘breath in life’. 

The Old Testament is a record of God’s transmission 
of his life and energy among his people. His universal 
spirit has first given life and then, as man has evolved 
and has become able to absorb it, a knowledge of God. 








